  "description": "COUSR01C applies NO case normalisation, and that is an asymmetry rather than an oversight: app/cbl/COSGN00C.cbl:132 and :135 wrap both USERIDI and PASSWDI in FUNCTION UPPER-CASE before comparing them, while COUSR01C contains the intrinsic zero times and simply MOVEs each field at :154-158. So a lower-case id, a mixed-case password, a lower-case type and lower-case names are all stored exactly as typed. Three independent assertions here break if an upper-casing 'tidy-up' is ever added: the eighty-byte record image, the confirmation text at :255-258 which reads back the stored id, and the row's POSITION in the key-sequenced final state - 'newusr01' begins with x'6E' and sorts after every seeded key, where 'NEWUSR01' begins with x'4E' and would sort into the middle. Do not harmonise this with sign-on.",
